## C. Exploration of the L1 rules

Runs: 3681; distinct final observations: 36.
Premises: P1 the command starts inside a caller's transaction; P2 an interactive operator commits at a halt; P3 the process ends between the outer TCOMMIT and SetCommitted.

| Rule | Meaning | Violations with no premise | Violations only under premises | Example shapes (mode, deps, activate, crash point) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| L1-REC-TOP | every command leaves one history record | 0 | {'P1-caller-transaction': 424, 'P3-commit-flag-window': 24} |  |
| L1-REC-DEP | every dependency load that started leaves a history record | 109 | {'P3-commit-flag-window': 28, 'P1-caller-transaction': 361} | ('dev', 'fail', 'fail', None); ('dev', 'fail', 'ok', None); ('txn', 'fail', 'fail', None); ('txn', 'fail', 'ok', None); ('txn', 'ok', 'fail', None); ('dev', 'fail', 'fail', 'activate') |
| L1-COMMIT-SOUND | Committed = 0 means none of the action's changes were kept | 82 | {'P2-operator-commits-at-halt': 372, 'P3-commit-flag-window': 44, 'P1-caller-transaction': 248} | ('dev', 'fail', 'fail', 'activate'); ('dev', 'fail', 'fail', 'before-dep'); ('dev', 'fail', 'fail', 'deps'); ('dev', 'fail', 'fail', 'guard'); ('dev', 'fail', 'fail', 'manifest'); ('dev', 'fail', 'ok', 'activate') |
| L1-COMMIT-EXACT | Committed = 1 means some change was kept (a load without a transaction may over-report) | 0 | 0 | |
| L1-SUCCESS-COMMITTED | a successful command is marked committed (top-level record) | 0 | 0 | |
| L1-ENDED | an end time is recorded exactly when the command ended normally | 0 | 0 | |
| L1-SUCCESS-EXACT | Success is recorded exactly when the command worked; never after a crash | 0 | 0 | |
| L1-ATOMIC | a failed or crashed transactional load leaves installed modules unchanged | 0 | {'P2-operator-commits-at-halt': 288, 'P3-commit-flag-window': 28, 'P1-caller-transaction': 192} |  |
| L1-DEV-KEEP | a developer-mode load keeps the module record once it is saved | 0 | {'P1-caller-transaction': 196, 'P3-commit-flag-window': 8} |  |
| L1-SUCCESS-STATE | a successful load installs the module and its dependencies | 0 | {'P1-caller-transaction': 6} |  |
| L1-REFUSE | a refused load changes no installed module | 0 | 0 | |
| L1-NO-TEMP | no temporary history record is left behind | 0 | 0 | |
| L1-PKG-NAMED | a record names the module once its manifest was read | 322 | {'P3-commit-flag-window': 8, 'P2-operator-commits-at-halt': 360, 'P1-caller-transaction': 270} | ('dev', 'fail', 'fail', None); ('dev', 'fail', 'ok', None); ('dev', 'halt', 'fail', None); ('dev', 'halt', 'ok', None); ('dev', 'none', 'fail', None); ('dev', 'none', 'ok', None) |

Without any crash (no halt injected), rules violated outside premises: L1-PKG-NAMED, L1-REC-DEP.

